& [Fault]
  + the first clean-target focused compile stopped in runner unit-test code because it imported a nonexistent remote-probe fixture helper omitted the existing controller fixture identity arguments and shadowed the mock-backend helper in one test

& [Containment]
  + compilation stopped before tests and the sealed production permit remained unconstructible
  + no OpenSSH invocation EVO-X2 contact provider request remote call or effect occurred

& [Resolution]
  + use the exact three-argument controller fixture construct and seal the existing public remote-probe form directly
  + rename the mock-backend helper so local values cannot shadow later fixture construction

& [Lesson]
  + new cross-crate tests must reuse the already-published fixture signatures and public sealers rather than infer convenience constructors
